  "operative_text": "Section 1 (C.R.S. 30-15-302(1)): AN AREA DESIGNATED PURSUANT TO THIS SECTION MUST HAVE THIRTY-FIVE DWELLINGS OR MORE PER SQUARE MILE. BEFORE ADOPTING A RESOLUTION TO DESIGNATE AN AREA PURSUANT TO THIS SUBSECTION (1), THE BOARD OF COUNTY COMMISSIONERS MAY CONSULT WITH THE SHERIFF AND CONSIDER THE SHERIFF'S RECOMMENDATION OF WHETHER TO ADOPT THE RESOLUTION.\nSection 1 (C.R.S. 30-15-302(1.5)): A RESOLUTION ENACTED PURSUANT TO THIS SECTION MAY NOT PROHIBIT DISCHARGE OF A FIREARM IN A DESIGNATED AREA: (a) BY A PEACE OFFICER ACTING WITHIN THE SCOPE OF THE OFFICER'S AUTHORITY AND IN THE PERFORMANCE OF THE OFFICER'S DUTIES; (b) IN AN INDOOR SHOOTING GALLERY LOCATED ENTIRELY WITHIN A PRIVATE RESIDENCE; (c) IN THE NORMAL LAWFUL OPERATION OR USE OF A QUALIFYING SPORT SHOOTING RANGE, AS DEFINED IN SECTION 25-12-109; (d) BY A PERSON ENGAGED IN A LAWFUL HUNTING ACTIVITY; (e) BY A PERSON ENGAGED IN LIVESTOCK MANAGEMENT; OR (f) PURSUANT TO A WILDLIFE MANAGEMENT ACTIVITY CONDUCTED BY A GOVERNMENT AGENCY, OR AS DESCRIBED IN SECTION 33-3-106 OR SECTION 33-6-107 (9)."
}